Proposed patch — NOT applied by ScoutSources (the L1 decides what lands).

Target: corpus/SOURCES.md (rows S346 and S349), at lane revision b96dc4beb8b826dab80ff07411b07c549c7a1b17.

Why: the round's own registry rows and the round's own entries disagree about which entry uses which row.

  * S346 (init/main.c) — row's used-by cell lists only corpus/knowledge/hibernation-boot-parse-r86.md,
    but corpus/knowledge/hibernation-availability-r85.md cites S346 twice (line 3, "S346 (init/main.c) … added
    round 86"; line 56, "pinned round 86 as S346 (raw 201-228)").
  * S349 (kernel/power/main.c) — the row's used-by cell lists corpus/knowledge/hibernation-availability-r85.md,
    and that entry does name S349 (lines 3 and 70), so the row is TRUE as it stands. The round that pinned the
    file is r86 (.ufo/waves/round-86/before/src/kernel_power_main.c, sha256
    7b60dabe707cf070b416f6375946c213b96bf3f67c3161b69c9a4fcfc9f53955) but the r86 entry does not cite S349 —
    a pinning fact, not a usage fact. Leaving S349 unchanged is correct; the note is recorded so the L1 does not
    "fix" it by adding the r86 entry to the used-by cell (that would BREAK the reverse-cite census command,
    which requires every used-by path to name the row id — the r86 entry does not name S349).

