S349 is deliberately NOT touched: its row is already true (its used-by entry names it), and adding the r86 entry
to that cell would break the reverse-cite census command, because the r86 entry does not name S349.

Census notes:
  * the seven frozen registry commands must stay clean (350 rows after the S350 candidate lands; malformed 0;
    tier/status enums unchanged; duplicate ids 0; used-by paths must exist on disk);
  * the reverse-cite command (awk … $12 | while read … grep -qw "$i" "$p") requires the used-by file to name the
    row id — hibernation-availability-r85.md names S346 (lines 3 and 56), so the added cell passes that check;
  * "no '|' inside any cell" holds: the cell above contains no pipe characters.
